 #:seon.task{:name "an-interpreted-callable-holds-its-definition-digest"
             :plan "(hybrid-test-results R3, owner decision 2026-10-12: methods are not declarations) A test whose body ran a callable with no definition digest (a `defmethod` body, a protocol extension, a fn bound to no declared Var) gets no reuse key, so `my.test/check` executes it again and never reuses its green. Verified on default (lane no-key, HEAD 3780e1107): a defmulti, a defmethod and a deftest calling it, as separate requests on an own-branch agent, then the method changed: `my.test/check` answers executed 0, reused 1, passed? true. Neither observation sees the method: `seon.instrument/wrap-interpreted` wraps only contracted definitions, so `seon.batch/executed` holds no key for a method body or a multimethod call, and the test row's `:seon.fn/calls` omits `area` because `seon.fn/analyze-forms` leaves an unresolved symbol out of the edges (kondo reports `:unresolved-symbol`). Done when `seon.test.runner/commit-results!` (through `seon.test.runner/executed-roots`) or `seon.test.runner/reach-digests` withholds the key of a result whose body ran such a callable; the producer is the first thing to decide, see the options in the lane report. Red proof (written, red on HEAD, applies to test/seon/test/redefined_callee_test.clj): docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/no-key-proof.patch, the deftest `a-test-that-ran-a-callable-with-no-definition-digest-reruns`. Cost: a test with no undeclared callable keeps `:seon.test/executed-count` 0 on a second check. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-test-results.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/r3-notes.md`."}
