 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-reading-task-tags-reruns-when-a-test-is-tagged"
             :plan "A Prove step's own proof (TASK-CHAIN §3b) reads the program it holds: `(seq (:seon.task/proofs (seon.task/task-edges (seon.db/db) successor)))`. `seon.test/select` keys its result by what its body executed (hybrid-test-results R2) and not by the tag facts it read, so after the agent tags a test with the successor the red is reused (`:seon.test/unchanged true`, executed 0) and the step can never end by itself: chain experiment 3 attempts 285fdccc2fa6 and 02110a533e26 were capped on it, and root rewrote the end. The owner ruled other cluster data unkeyed (hybrid-test-results §2); a test tag is a program fact on the test entity. Root decides the producer before this is assigned: the step proof takes the held step's branch commit as a declared input (the decision of `seon.context/a-step-proof-cannot-observe-its-agents-test-evidence`), the key includes the `:seon.task/tasks` facts of the tests a body read, or the Prove step's done is derived from its product alone, with no step proof (chain experiment 2's G1, being fixed by lane g1). Read `seon.context/step-status`, `seon.task/task-edges`, `seon.test.runner/reach-digests`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-3.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-test-results.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "since-previous-run-narrowing-has-no-production-caller"
